{"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","data":{"body":"Related observation (local host, not the server), 2026-10-19 PDT: a local CLI close (talented-portable-sow) spawned the detached compaction worker (compact_trigger.run_sweep, pid 56766). It was reparented to PID 1 within 37 s and ran about 4 minutes before exiting on its own. Its stand-aside guard checks the store lock only BEFORE it starts, so once running it holds the lock for the whole sweep. That matches the server-side 'compact-sweep held=93s' holder that made an MCP create_ticket fail after waiting 181 s (earlier comment). Not established: whether a sweep was involved in the divergence itself."},"env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1792387189708480001,"uuid":"ed14aecf-da50-4459-90b2-b06ccff0e79f"}